# tilc.til - a TIL compiler written in TIL ("TIL Core" subset, see selfhost/README.md)
#
#   til run --vm selfhost/tilc.til input.til output.tbc
#   til build --target vm selfhost/tilc.til -o tilc.tbc
#   tilvm tilc.tbc input.til output.tbc          (any TIL VM, e.g. a calculator)
#
# Produces .tbc bytecode v2 - the same bytes as `til build --target vm`
# (src/til.py). The structure mirrors the Python front end (Lexer, Parser,
# SemanticChecker, BytecodeCompiler, TBCModule.to_bytes) so that both accept
# the same syntax and emit the same instructions, constants and line tables.
#
# Memory: tokens are streamed (only a small look-ahead window is kept); the
# first pass parses the whole file but keeps only declarations; the second
# pass re-reads each function body from its saved source position. Statements
# are compiled while they are parsed (only expressions become trees); the
# bytecode is kept as bytes (strings), only its last few hundred bytes in an
# array; operator chains are folded and compiled with loops. Integers are
# handled as 16-bit limbs so the compiler gives the same result on 32-bit and
# 64-bit VMs; float literals and float constant folding use exact integer
# arithmetic (no host floats are used).

# ── token types (names in TT_NAMES, as in TokenType of src/til.py) ──────────
